  "caveats": [
    "static_analysis.py:86 caps suspicious_strings at MAX_SUSPICIOUS_STRINGS=25 and iterates STRING_PATTERNS in url, ip, shell order \u2014 so an APK with >=25 distinct URL matches records zero ip-kind and zero shell-kind strings. 84/668 (12.6%) of cached outputs sit at that cap, including 23/360 malicious. Every per-APK indicator count is therefore right-censored at 25.",
    "A 'network host indicator' here is any http(s):// string or dotted-quad match found in the DEX string pool. It is not evidence of a C2 channel and is not evidence the host was ever contacted. This audit measures joinability, not malice.",
    "bridge/matcher.py compares c2_host by exact equality against the RAW suspicious_strings value, not against a parsed hostname. A ground-truth c2_host recorded as a hostname can therefore never match a url-kind indicator (whose value is the full URL). Only kind=='ip' values (bare dotted quads) and a ground-truth entry holding the byte-identical full URL can join today. 10.6% of malicious APKs (38/360) carry at least one ip-kind indicator.",
    "banking_holdout n=16 is reported for completeness only; it is underpowered for any rate claim."
  ]
}